Source: gnome-remote-desktop-gdm-hwenc
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: gnome-remote-desktop-gdm-hwenc
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, acl
Enhances: gnome-remote-desktop
Description: hardware-accelerated encode for the GDM login screen (Rockchip)
 gnome-remote-desktop can hardware-encode the RDP stream on Rockchip RK3588
 via the MPP video codec. This package installs a udev rule that grants the
 GDM greeter's dynamic per-session user, a member of group "gdm", access to
 the MPP device nodes (/dev/mpp_service, the DMA-heaps, /dev/rga), so the
 pre-login greeter is hardware-accelerated too and not just the logged-in
 session, which is already covered by the "video" group.
 .
 It is a separate, opt-in package and is not pulled in by gnome-remote-desktop
 because it widens access to the video codec hardware to the whole "gdm" group.
 Install it only if you want the login screen hardware-encoded.
